---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy — CyberPatate" 
  description="Privacy policy for CyberPatate software and flight simulation tools (AlphaFloor EFB and XLauncher)."
>
  <div class="legal-page-wrapper section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-card glass-panel">
        <header class="legal-header">
          <span class="section-tag green">Transparency</span>
          <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="legal-updated">Last Updated: October 14, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <article class="legal-content">
          <section>
            <h2>1. Our Privacy Philosophy</h2>
            <p>
              At <strong>CyberPatate</strong>, we believe software running on your computer should respect your machine, your network, and your data. <strong>We do not collect, track, monetize, or sell your flight simulator sessions, personal files, or browsing behavior.</strong>
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>2. Information We Process (and What Stays Local)</h2>
            <h3>A. Local Simulator Data & Tablet Streaming</h3>
            <p>
              When you fly with <strong>AlphaFloor EFB</strong>, all flight telemetry, datarefs, performance calculations, and weight & balance numbers are processed <strong>100% locally on your computer</strong>. The embedded tablet web server serves pages directly across your home Wi-Fi local area network (LAN). No simulator state is ever streamed to cloud servers.
            </p>

            <h3>B. License Verification & Device Node Locking</h3>
            <p>
              To enforce our fair 3-machine activation policy, our software computes a one-way cryptographic hash of local machine hardware identifiers:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>This fingerprint contains no personal information, usernames, IP addresses, or file paths.</li>
              <li>It is used solely to verify active machine activation slots against our secure licensing server.</li>
              <li>Once activated, license signatures are verified locally and offline without requiring continuous internet pings while you fly.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>C. Optional Third-Party Services</h3>
            <p>
              If you choose to use integrated pilot utilities:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>SimBrief</strong>: Your pilot username is used strictly to query the SimBrief dispatch API to download your flight plan.</li>
              <li><strong>Navigraph</strong>: OAuth authentication tokens are stored securely on your local device and communicate directly with Navigraph endpoints for chart retrieval.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>3. Payment Processing</h2>
            <p>
              All online purchases are processed securely through <strong>Stripe</strong>. CyberPatate does not receive, process, or store credit card numbers, bank details, or CVV codes. Payment transactions are governed by Stripe's industry-certified security protocols and privacy policy.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>4. Website Hosting & Analytics</h2>
            <p>
              This website is delivered via high-availability static Edge CDN infrastructure (GitHub Pages). We do not use third-party tracking pixels, marketing cookies, or invasive analytics. Standard server request metadata is processed solely for network routing, security, and DDoS mitigation.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>5. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
              If you have any questions or data requests regarding this Privacy Policy, please reach out to us directly:
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href="mailto:contact@cyberpatate.fr">contact@cyberpatate.fr</a>
            </p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-wrapper {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .legal-card {
    max-width: 840px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3.5rem;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-content section {
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .legal-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--hud-cyan);
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-content p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-content li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal-card {
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
